<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franconian Circle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a>–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franconian Circle was one of the Imperial Circles into which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> was divided from 1500. It grouped the territories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, including the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eichstatt">Eichstätt</a>, the Hohenzollern margraviates, imperial cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> and many small counties. Its assembly organised troop contingents for imperial defence, supervised coinage and roads, and kept the peace among its members until the Empire ended in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franconian-circle.jpg" alt="Franconian Circle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Franconia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
